{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>After the death</b> — it is written above: \"and to a man who lies with a menstruating woman,\" and adjacent to it: \"after the death\" — a hint to what they said: one who engages in relations with a pure woman and a menstruant spread beneath him — he must not withdraw while the organ is alive, but must wait until the organ dies and then withdraw. And furthermore it is written above: \"this is the law of,\" and adjacent to it: \"after the death\" — teaches that they died for issuing a halakhic ruling in the presence of their teacher. And furthermore it is written above: \"My Tabernacle that is among them,\" and adjacent to it: \"after the death\" — a hint to what is stated: \"through those near Me I will be sanctified.\" And the portion of Yom HaKippurim is juxtaposed to the portion of the menstruant, to say: just as the menstruant sits seven days before she purifies, so too for Yom HaKippurim they separate the high priest seven days before he enters inside."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:32.693916444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}